{"id": "86252", "name": "Parabola_1", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p>The equation given below represents a parabola: \\[ {{CT:0}}. \\] <br /> Find the coordinates of the vertex, \\((x_c,y_c)\\), the coordinates of the focus, \\((x_f,y_f)\\) and the equation of the directrix.</p>\n<p>Give your answer as a list containing (in this order) the coordinates of the vertex, the coordinates of the focus and the equation of the directrix.<br /> \\( [ x_c, y_c, x_f, y_f, eq ] \\) = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>", "generalfeedback": "<p>If the equation can be written in the form \\[ (y - y_c) = a\\cdot(x-x_c)^2,\\] then the vertex is given by \\((x_c,y_c)\\), the focus is given by \\((x_c, y_c +\\frac{1}{4a})\\), and the directrix by \\(y = y_c - \\frac{1}{4a}\\).</p>\n<p><br /> Or, if it can be written in the form \\[ (x - x_c) = a\\cdot(y-y_c)^2,\\] then the vertex is given by \\((x_c,y_c)\\), the focus is given by \\((x_c + \\frac{1}{4a}, y_c)\\), and the directrix by \\(x = x_c - \\frac{1}{4a}\\). <br /> <br /> The equation \\({{CT:0}}\\)    can be written as:</p>\n<p>\\[ {{CT:1}}{{CT:2}} = ({{CT:3}}) . \\]</p>\n<p>Giving, \\(a = {{CT:1}}\\), the coordinates of the vertex are  \\(({{CT:4}},{{CT:5}})\\), the coordinates of the focus are \\(({{CT:6}},{{CT:7}})\\) and the directrix is \\({{CT:8}}\\).</p>\n<p> </p>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidatio